      "description": "A coalition of EU member states, frustrated by the slow pace of the Sovereign Compute Corridor and distrustful of hyperscaler commitments, quietly launches a parallel initiative to federate national cloud resources into a 'sovereign cloud alliance' for AI workloads. The effort leverages existing national AI strategies and security certifications, aiming to create a minimally viable alternative to U.S.-controlled infrastructure by mid-2033. It operates outside formal EU channels, mirroring the northern runtime alliance's fragmentation but focused on compute sovereignty.",
